// Function Curve List, in the format:
// {
//	    STRING
//
//  	INT
//
//	DOUBLE*
// }
//
// The '{' signals the start of a curve definition
// The STRING is the name of the curve.
// The INT is the number of keys in the curve
// The DOUBLE* is a list of DOUBLE values:  alternating time and value pairs.  For example, if the curve contained
// 1 key, the keys section would have 2 values - the first being the key's time, the second being the key's value,
// like so:  time_1 value_1 time_2 value_2 time_3 value_3 ... time_n value_n
// Therefore, the number of actual DOUBLE values in the key section will always be 2 * Num. Keys
// Some game engines, namely the Unreal engine, have hard limits on string sizes (1024 bytes in Unreal's case).
// Therefore, the keys section is segmented into seperate lines, each containing 25 keys (time / value pairs).
// The '}' signals the end of a curve definition
//
// There are Num. Curves of these curve definition entries.

